The '''first season''' of ''[[Dancing with the Stars (American TV series)|Dancing with the Stars]]'' debuted on [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] on June 1, 2005. Six celebrities were paired with six professional ballroom dancers. [[Tom Bergeron]] and [[Lisa Canning]] were the hosts while [[Carrie Ann Inaba]], [[Len Goodman]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]] were the three judges for this season.

The premiere drew over 13 million viewers, the second biggest summer debut ever for an American reality series after ''[[Survivor (American TV series)|Survivor]]''.<ref>{{cite news | last = Associated Press | title = 'Dancing With the Stars' Debuts in 2nd Place | work = FoxNews | date = 2005-06-08 | url = https://www.foxnews.com/story/dancing-with-the-stars-debuts-in-2nd-place | access-date = 2009-05-06 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20080414041316/http://www.foxnews.com/story/0,2933,158923,00.html | archive-date = 2008-04-14 | url-status = live }}</ref> The second week climbed to 15 million viewers, and the show climbed to the top of the ratings in the summer 2005 TV season, where it remained for the remainder of the season.<ref>{{cite news | last = Maynard | first = John | title = ABC Cuts In: 'Dancing' Racks Up No. 1 Summer Ratings | newspaper = The Washington Post | date = 2005-07-13 | url = https://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2005/07/12/AR2005071201440.html | access-date = 2009-05-06 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20121108000601/http://www.washingtonpost.com/wp-dyn/content/article/2005/07/12/AR2005071201440.html | archive-date = 2012-11-08 | url-status = live }}</ref>

The season finale aired on July 6, 2005, where ''[[General Hospital]]'' actress [[Kelly Monaco]] and [[Alec Mazo]] were announced as the winners,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://people.com/celebrity/kelly-monaco-wins-dancing-with-the-stars/|title=Kelly Monaco Wins Dancing with the Stars|date=July 7, 2005|work=peoplecelebrity.com|access-date=May 20, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171113131250/http://people.com/celebrity/kelly-monaco-wins-dancing-with-the-stars/|archive-date=November 13, 2017|url-status=live}}</ref> while actor [[John O'Hurley]] and [[Charlotte Jørgensen]] finished in second place.

Due to controversy over Kelly Monaco winning over the consistently higher-scoring John O'Hurley, a special rematch episode was held on September 20, 2005, with the results announced on a September 22 telecast. This time, John O'Hurley and Charlotte Jørgensen were the champions, and sizable donations were made to both Monaco and O'Hurley's chosen charities.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pierce |first=Scott D. |date=2005-08-02 |title=ABC, 'Dancing' winner sidestepping criticism |url=https://www.deseret.com/2005/8/2/19905015/abc-dancing-winner-sidestepping-criticism |access-date=2023-10-25 |website=Deseret News |language=en |archive-date=October 25, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231025234049/https://www.deseret.com/2005/8/2/19905015/abc-dancing-winner-sidestepping-criticism |url-status=live }}</ref><ref name=":0">{{cite web|url=https://www.today.com/popculture/rematch-gave-dancing-its-rhythm-back-wbna9444985|title=Rematch gave 'Dancing' its rhythm back|date=September 22, 2005|work=today.com}}</ref><ref name=":1">{{cite web|url=https://www.eonline.com/news/50494/monaco-o-hurley-dancing-rematch/|title=Monaco, O'Hurley: "Dancing" Rematch!|date=August 18, 2005|work=eonline.com|access-date=September 28, 2020|archive-date=September 17, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200917091807/https://www.eonline.com/news/50494/monaco-o-hurley-dancing-rematch|url-status=live}}</ref>

